## Summary

Adds a durable engineering-memory system under `docs/engineering/` so future sessions can continue KV cache / KV offload work without depending on chat history.

The documentation separates:

- mutable current state;
- chronological PR history;
- searchable incident/root-cause records;
- expensive hardware/integration validation evidence;
- point-in-time handoffs.

## Initial coverage

Records the current and historical work around:

- PR #3 workload fairness and tokenizer convergence;
- PR #5 cache eviction/restore pressure benchmark and its current draft continuation state;
- recompute vs filesystem restore crossover measurements;
- PR #7 shadow cost model design, exact source-over-wheel integration, hardware anchors, p256 adaptive crossover, final validation, and merge;
- fake `vllm` nested-newline fixture failure;
- transient `metrics_before` connection refusal investigation;
- `benchmarks/cache` Ruff/format/SPDX/markdownlint baseline;
- GitHub -> Gitee -> Pod synchronization/write-path constraints.

## Scope

Documentation only. Final compare against `main` reports:

- 15 added Markdown files;
- 2960 additions / 0 deletions;
- 0 runtime, benchmark, test, config, or workflow changes;
- `behind_by=0`.

## Validation

Final head: `8e45f1a97e7e0c8df589291f2466545d376fd599`.

Repository Actions on the final head established:

- pre-run-check: PASS;
- markdownlint for all new `docs/engineering/**` files and the new engineering-history spec/plan: PASS after fixing the PR-local table/heading findings;
- typos: PASS;
- actionlint: PASS;
- mypy Python 3.10: PASS;
- mypy Python 3.11: PASS;
- mypy Python 3.12: PASS;
- mypy Python 3.13: PASS;
- shell lint and the remaining non-cache hooks: PASS.

The aggregate `pre-commit --all-files` job remains red solely because it exercises pre-existing `benchmarks/cache` baseline debt already present on `main`:

- Ruff/E501 and Ruff-format changes in existing cache benchmark Python files;
- missing SPDX headers in 16 existing cache benchmark Python files;
- MD060 table-spacing errors in `benchmarks/cache/README.md:52`.

No auto-fixes to those baseline files are included in this documentation PR. The baseline is documented explicitly in `docs/engineering/incidents/cache-benchmark-ci-baseline.md` so it can be resolved as a separate scoped workstream.
